recommended_stack:
Environment: native Windows, Python 3.12.10, using `<python.exe> -m uv`. CPU-only torch from PyPI is the default. Verified with `uv pip compile --python-platform x86_64-pc-windows-msvc`: beat-this==1.1.0, all-in-one-infer==3.1.0, librosa==1.0.0, soundfile>=0.14, scipy and numpy resolve into a 66-package lock. Key pins: torch==2.15.0, torchaudio==2.11.1, demucs-infer==4.4.0, madmom-infer==0.2.0, numba==0.68.1, rotary-embedding-torch==0.9.2. The lock is at C:\Users\OPENSR~1\AppData\Local\Temp\claude\18e41bb73b27f8e3\cfc48f00-d046-409f-8e46-ef42c153038f\scratchpad\research\rhythm-structure\stack_recommended.txt. Pin all-in-one-infer and its sibling packages to a git commit SHA, because openmirlab no longer publishes to PyPI; keep PyPI 3.1.0 as the fallback. Optional extra: mir_eval==0.8.2 for agreement metrics (MIT, pure Python).

Pipeline:
0) Decode once with ffmpeg 9.0.2 (not soundfile or torchaudio) to a canonical 44.1 kHz stereo float32 WAV, plus a mono copy. Capture ffmpeg warnings into source.decode_warnings. Every tool reads this file or array, so all timestamps share one clock. Verified this session: Versatile.flac has a corrupt FLAC frame. libsndfile aborts with 'flac decoder lost sync'; ffmpeg reports the error and continues.
1) Stems: HTDemucs 4-stem (bass, drums, other, vocals) via demucs-infer 4.4.0. Reuse the stems from the stems/instruments track if they exist; this is the most expensive step on CPU, about 45-90 s.
2) Beats: beat_this.inference.Audio2Frames('final0', device='cpu') on the mix gives beat and downbeat logits at 50 fps; save them. Then use the minimal postprocessor for beats and downbeats, and beat_this.utils.infer_beat_numbers for bar positions. Optional: when the inter-beat interval varies by less than 3%, rerun the postprocessing as a DBN (beats_per_bar [3,4]) through madmom-infer for a cleaner grid.
3) Structure: allin1_infer.AllInOneSession(model='harmonix-all', device='cpu') with stems_input from step 1, include_activations=True and include_embeddings=True. This yields segments and labels, the 10-class label softmax and boundary activation at 100 fps, BPM, and a second beat/downbeat set.
4) DSP features (librosa 1.0.0): onset_strength_multi over the viz band rule (bass 32-150, mid 150-2200, high 2200-16000 Hz) on the mix and on the drums stem; onset_detect(backtrack=True); tempogram, metrogram and PLP for local tempo and its clarity; feature.tempo with a log-normal prior as tempo estimator C; beat-synchronous CQT chroma and MFCC. In parallel, port the viz/js/audio.js kick envelope and ACF tempo so kick strengths match the live visualiser.
5) Custom fusion, a pure numpy module:
- tempo arbitration across the beat_this IBI, allin1 BPM and librosa/ACF estimates, classifying their ratios as 1, 2, 1/2, 3/2, 2/3, 4/3 or 3/4;
- beat refinement (parabolic peak interpolation on the logits, then snapping to a transient within ±25 ms);
- a piecewise-constant tempo grid and the tempo curve;
- meter and irregular bars;
- 4/8/16-bar phrases;
- snapping section boundaries to downbeats and merging segments shorter than 2 bars;
- repetition groups (cosine similarity of segment-mean chroma, MFCC and allin1 embeddings, then agglomerative grouping);
- bar-level energy, bass, kick-count and onset-density features, used to detect drops, build-ups, breakdowns and pre-drop gaps;
- the confidence model and QA flags;
- a merged, prioritised cue sheet.
6) Optional: SongFormer in a separate venv for a better label pass on vocal pop (adds pre-chorus); onnxruntime or ROCm for speed.
7) Emit rhythm_structure.json plus float16 curve sidecars, and review files: Audacity label tracks for beats, downbeats, sections and drops, and a click/boundary-cue sonified preview (allin1_infer.sonify, or our own clicks) so a person can listen to and view the grid.

Estimated CPU time for a 4-minute song on the 9800X3D: about 1.5-3 minutes in total with HTDemucs (decode under 1 s, HTDemucs 45-90 s, beat_this 3-10 s, allin1 8 folds 20-50 s, librosa 5-10 s plus a one-time numba JIT, fusion under 2 s). About 40-70 s if the stems are reused. These timings are estimates; torch was not installed, per the task rules.
